 {"id":"GAP-004","status":"complete","priority":"P2","type":"bug","complexity":3,"title":"P2 — ralph-loop has no exit path: 32 orphaned loops poll their state DB forever and hold 1.87 GB","reasoning":"PM cycle 2026-11-17 (pass 10; hunter-verified live measurement, source-confirmed at tip 874a42d1). MEASURED at 13:00Z on this host: 32 ralph-loop processes alive across 7 distinct trees — 14 in /home/kara/speclang, 8 in worktrees/speclang-QA-SPECLANG-5-R6, 3 in worktrees/speclang-QA-SPECLANG-5-R3, 3 in /home/kara/SpecLang, 1 in worktrees/speclang-UX-002, 1 in worktrees/speclang-README-SWEEP, 1 in speclang/.tmp/freshclone. Every one has ppid 7126 = systemd --user, meaning its launching agent session exited and the loop was reparented instead of stopping. All 32 sit in state Sl at wchan ep_poll with 0.0% CPU and 0-3s cumulative CPU each (sum 18 CPU-seconds for the whole set) while holding 1,873 MB RSS; oldest etime 3h58m. SOURCE: src/ralph-loop.ts:238-247 sets isRunning=true and runs `while (this.isRunning)`, sleeping 5000ms whenever getNextTask() returns null, and isRunning is assigned nowhere else (grep -n isRunning returns only :203 false and :238 true) — there is no SIGTERM/SIGINT handler, no launcher-liveness check, no heartbeat and no idle bound (grep -nE 'ppid|parent|process.kill|SIGTERM|SIGHUP|orphan|heartbeat' src/ralph-loop.ts returns 0 hits). The only exits are an uncaught error (process.exit(1) in main's catch) or an external SIGKILL, so each orphan keeps polling its SQLite state DB every 5 seconds indefinitely. No host reaper covers this class: ~/.hermes/scripts holds docker-orphan-audit.py, forkbomb-reaper.py, staging-reaper.sh, state-db-reaper.py, stray-duckbrain-reaper.py and worker-scope-reaper.py, none of which targets ralph-loop. CORRECTION TO AN EARLIER ATTRIBUTION ON THIS BOARD: these orphans are a memory/lifecycle leak, NOT the host-load source — 18 CPU-seconds spread over 4 hours cannot produce loadavg 34-50. At measurement time the load was carried by bun test at 97.3% (1h39m), schedulerd at 38.9%, duckbrain http at 22.1%, cost-exporter at 12.2%, warpfs/duckdb cc1plus builds and a sqlite quick_check running 1h16m, with only 6 processes in R state. A later pass must not park this row on load grounds, and must not expect reaping these 32 to lower loadavg.","acceptance_criteria":"(1) cd /home/kara/speclang && npx vitest run tests/db/ralph-loop-lifecycle.test.ts exits 0, and that new test file asserts BOTH exits: SIGTERM delivered during idle polling ends start() within 2s, and a dead/absent launcher (or an expired idle bound) ends start() within 2s. (2) cd /home/kara/speclang && grep -cE 'SIGTERM|SIGINT' src/ralph-loop.ts prints 1 or more, quoted in the completion event as the installed signal path. (3) cd /home/kara/speclang && npx vitest run tests/db/ralph-loop-fresh-state.test.ts exits 0, so the existing ralph state-DB contract stays green. The completion event must name the chosen orphan predicate (parent-pid liveness vs heartbeat/TTL vs bounded idle) and must state that the 32 pre-existing orphans are host residue to be reaped by the operator/harness, not proof of this change.","detail":{"metadata":{"fingerprint":"764fd442d18c90016ba3486f70d911ba5bec4530fb4f7538887562a471d1634c","measured_at":"2026-11-17T13:00:00Z","tip":"874a42d1","orphan_count":32,"rss_mb":1873,"cpu_seconds_total":18,"trees":7},"evidence":[{"cmd":"ps -eo pid,args --no-headers | grep -F 'ralph-loop.ts' | grep -v -F 'grep -F' | wc -l","out":"32"},{"cmd":"ps -eo rss,args --no-headers | grep -F 'ralph-loop.ts' | grep -v -F 'grep -F' | awk '{s+=$1} END {print s\" KB\"}'","out":"1918656 KB"},{"cmd":"for p in 829885 949914 1079435; do cat /proc/$p/wchan; done","out":"ep_poll / ep_poll / ep_poll"},{"cmd":"ps -o pid,ppid,args -p 7126 --no-headers","out":"7126 1 /usr/lib/systemd/systemd --user --deserialize=107"},{"cmd":"grep -n 'isRunning' src/ralph-loop.ts","out":"203: private isRunning: boolean = false; / 238: this.isRunning = true; (no other a